Consider a system with processes P1, P2. X is a Binary semaphore variable with an initial value of 1 and count is a variable with initial value of 1.

The processes P1, P2 executes routines P1(), P2() for accessing critical section.

P1() {
  DOWN(X);
  count++;
  UP(X);
}
P2() {
  DOWN(X);
  count--;
  UP(X);
}

Which of the following statements(S1, S2, S3) is/are TRUE?

S1: The maximum value of count can be infinite.
S2: The system cannot guarantee progress.
S3: The system does not provide Mutual Exclusion.

(A) S1 only (B) S1 and S3 (C) S2 and S3 (D) S1, S2, S3

Consider the function fun() which deletes the duplicate elements on a non-empty sorted single linked list.

typedef struct SL {
  int data;
  struct SL *next;
} SLL;

void fun(SLL *first) {
  SLL *curr = first, *temp;
  if (!curr)
    return;
  while (curr->next) {
    temp = curr->next;
    if (curr->data == temp->data)
      curr->next = temp->next;
    else
      curr = curr->next;
    free(temp);
  }
}

If first node address is passed to fun(), Fill in the blanks.

(A) curr temp temp next
(B) curr curr=curr->next
(C) temp curr=curr->next
(D) temp temp=temp->next

